// Jest Snapshot v1, https://goo.gl/fbAQLP

exports[`all rule hover preview renders a reviewable card for every catalog rule 1`] = `
"## \`invalid-capture-group-name\`

❌ **Error**

Capture group name \\"user\\\\_name\\" is invalid. Start with a letter and use only letters and numbers.

**Fix** — Use PPL named groups in the form \`(?<name>...)\`. Start each name with a letter and use only letters and numbers.

**Quick fix available** — \`username\`

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/rex/#parameters)

---

## \`unsupported-window-function-in-eventstats\`

❌ **Error**

Window function \\"rank\\" is not supported in eventstats/streamstats. Only row\\\\_number is supported.

**Fix** — Use \`row_number()\` for a window value, or choose an aggregation supported by \`eventstats\` or \`streamstats\`, such as \`avg()\`.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/eventstats/#aggregation-functions)

---

## \`dedup-consecutive-unsupported\`

⚠️ **Warning**

consecutive=true uses an older query engine and may make this query slower.

**Fix** — Remove \`consecutive=true\` to use regular deduplication. No equivalent option preserves consecutive-only behavior.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/limitation/#unsupported-functionalities)

---

## \`replace-wildcard-asymmetry\`

❌ **Error**

The replace match has 2 \\"\\\\*\\" wildcards, but the replacement has 1. The counts must match.

**Fix** — Use the same number of \`*\` wildcards in the match and replacement patterns.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/replace/#limitations)

---

## \`union-min-datasets\`

❌ **Error**

The union command requires at least two datasets.

**Fix** — Add another dataset to \`union\`, or remove \`union\` when using only one dataset.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/)

---

## \`multisearch-min-subsearch\`

❌ **Error**

The multisearch command requires at least two subsearches.

**Fix** — Add a second subsearch, or run the single subsearch as a normal query.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/multisearch/#limitations)

---

## \`disabled-join-type\`

⚠️ **Warning**

A \\"cross\\" join can produce one result row for every pair of input rows and is disabled by default.

**Fix** — Use an \`inner\` or \`left\` join when it preserves the intended result. Otherwise, ask an administrator to enable \`plugins.calcite.all_join_types.allowed\`.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/join/#limitations)

---

## \`head-without-sort\`

ℹ️ **Info**

Without sort, head can return different rows each time the query runs.

**Fix** — Add \`sort\` before \`head\` when you need stable top or bottom results.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/head/)

---

## \`field-validation\`

❌ **Error**

Unknown field \\"reveneu\\". Did you mean \\"revenue\\"?

**Fix** — Correct the field name or PPL syntax. PPL runs commands left to right, so define a new field with \`eval\` before referencing it in a later command.

**Quick fix available** — \`revenue\`

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/fields/)

---

## \`expand-on-non-array\`

⚠️ **Warning**

Field \\"status\\" may contain only one value, so expand may have nothing to split into rows.

**Fix** — Use \`expand\` only with a field that contains multiple values. Otherwise, remove it.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/expand/#limitations)

---

## \`wildcard-source-zero-match\`

ℹ️ **Info**

Source pattern \\"lgos-\\\\*\\" matches no known index.

**Details** — Checked 47 visible indices.

**Fix** — Correct the \`source=\` pattern or choose an existing index.

**Quick fix available** — \`\` \`logs-2026.07.25\` \`\`

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/search/)

---

## \`division-by-zero\`

⚠️ **Warning**

Dividing by zero returns no value (null) instead of an error.

**Fix** — Use the intended divisor, or handle zero before dividing, for example \`if(total = 0, 0, errors / total)\`.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/functions/expressions/#arithmetic-operators)

---

## \`agg-on-text\`

⚠️ **Warning**

avg cannot calculate a number from text field \\"message\\", so it returns no value (null).

**Fix** — Use a numeric field, or convert numeric text to a number before applying \`avg\`, \`sum\`, or a similar function.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/functions/aggregations/)

---

## \`flat-object-subfield\`

❌ **Error**

PPL cannot search \\"attributes.region\\" because it is stored inside the flat\\\\_object field \\"attributes\\".

**Fix** — Use another field or query this data with DQL or the Search API. To use it in PPL, map and reindex it as a regular object field.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/mappings/supported-field-types/flat-object/#limitations)

---

## \`type-mismatch-numeric\`

⚠️ **Warning**

Field \\"status\\\\_code\\" is numeric, but \\"error\\" is not a number, so the comparison returns no rows.

**Fix** — Compare the field with a number, such as \`500\`, or use the text field that contains the value you want.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/functions/conversion/#string-to-numeric-type-conversion)

---

## \`enabled-false-object\`

⚠️ **Warning**

Field \\"metadata.trace\\\\_id\\" is stored but not searchable, so PPL returns null for it.

**Fix** — Query an indexed field instead. To make this value searchable, enable indexing in the mapping and reindex the data.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/mappings/mapping-parameters/enabled/#disabling-object-fields)

---

## \`rex-scan-cost\`

ℹ️ **Info**

rex runs the pattern against every input row from text field \\"body\\", even when it finds no match.

**Fix** — Filter out rows that cannot match the pattern before extraction, using time or an indexed field.

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/ppl/commands/rex/)

---

## \`operation-not-pushed\`

⚠️ **Warning**

This filter runs after the index scan, so rows it rejects are still read and returned to the PPL engine.

**Details** — Affected field: \`age\`. Comparison value: \`30\`.

**Fix** — Rewrite the highlighted operation with indexed fields and supported functions so the PPL engine can include it in the index request.

**Quick fix available** — \`age > 32\`

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/limitation/)

---

## \`operation-pushed-as-script\`

ℹ️ **Info**

OpenSearch evaluates this filter as a script for every candidate document instead of using a native index query.

**Details** — Affected field: \`age\`. Comparison value: \`30\`.

**Fix** — Use a direct field comparison or sort on an indexed field so OpenSearch can use a native query or field sort.

**Quick fix available** — \`age > 32\`

[Learn more →](https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/sql-and-ppl/limitation/)"
`;
